.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-FIRSTBOOT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-firstboot
.Nd finish an installed kldload machine at its first boot, for its profile
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa kldload-firstboot.service
runs
.Nm
once, at the first boot of an installed machine; it is not meant to be
run by hand.
It reads the profile from the install manifest and finishes what the
installer could not do from outside the running system:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
the persistent journal, the ZFS debug-message drain, and the key the host
uses to reach its own virtual machines;
.It
healing nets that install again anything the install-time transaction
missed \(em optional packages, the web view's libraries, swap, desktop
applications, the NVIDIA driver;
.It
the Secure Boot signing key made the same as the enrolled machine owner
key, and the ZFSBootMenu command line that keeps nouveau away from an
NVIDIA card;
.It
Grafana, the storage profile's shares, and the platform packages' version
locks;
.It
the profile's own role \(em a hypervisor, storage, monitoring, a desktop
\(em and restoring virtual machines at every boot where the profile runs
them.
.El
.Pp
Every failure it does not expect is logged with its line and command, and
fails the unit, so that it shows in
.Ql systemctl --failed
as well as in the log.
Steps that are allowed to fail say so where they are.
.Xr kldload-autodeploy 8
runs after it.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print what it does and exit 0, running nothing; any other argument is
exit 2.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /etc/kldload/install-manifest.env
The profile and what was asked for.
.It Pa /var/log/kldload/firstboot.log
Everything it did, and the line of any failure.
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/firstboot-done
Present once it has finished.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when done; 1 on a failure, logged with its line; 2 when given an
argument.
.Sh EXAMPLES
What went wrong at a first boot; not run for this page:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# systemctl status kldload-firstboot
# grep -E 'ERR:|FATAL|WARNING' /var/log/kldload/firstboot.log
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload-apply-platform-holds 8 ,
.Xr kldload-autodeploy 8 ,
.Xr kldload-mok-repair 8 ,
.Xr kldload-ollama-install 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-06-13 a desktop came up half built with nothing to say why; every
unexpected failure has named its line since.
Until 2026-09-30
.Fl -help
ran a first boot.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
On dnf systems it both enables a security-only update timer and masks
dnf-automatic; which of the two applies depends on the distribution's unit
names, and on a Fedora 44 desktop neither runs.
